  "claim": "Edith Louisa Cavell  was the woman whose execution for treason by German firing squad was the reason for Prussian Generalleutnant (Lieutenant General) Traugott von Sauberzweig's replacement as Military Governor of Brussels in 1915.",
  "evidencia": "Page: Traugott von Sauberzweig. Sentence: Traugott Martin von Sauberzweig (October 28, 1863 to April 14, 1920 in Kassel) was a Prussian \"Generalleutnant\" (Lieutenant General) who served on both the Eastern and Western Front in the German Army during World War I.\nPage: Traugott von Sauberzweig. Sentence: In 1915 he had been Military Governor of Brussels in the days of Edith Cavell's execution, and in connection with this tragedy his name was prominently mentioned.\nPage: Traugott von Sauberzweig. Sentence: The Cavell case was the reason that von Sauberzweig was supplanted.\nPage: Edith Cavell. Sentence: Edith Louisa Cavell ( ; 4 December 1865 – 12 October 1915) was a British nurse.\nPage: Edith Cavell. Sentence: She was accused of treason, found guilty by a court-martial and sentenced to death.\nPage: Edith Cavell. Sentence: Despite international pressure for mercy, she was shot by a German firing squad.",
  "evidence_text": "Page: Traugott von Sauberzweig. Sentence: Traugott Martin von Sauberzweig (October 28, 1863 to April 14, 1920 in Kassel) was a Prussian \"Generalleutnant\" (Lieutenant General) who served on both the Eastern and Western Front in the German Army during World War I.\nPage: Traugott von Sauberzweig. Sentence: In 1915 he had been Military Governor of Brussels in the days of Edith Cavell's execution, and in connection with this tragedy his name was prominently mentioned.\nPage: Traugott von Sauberzweig. Sentence: The Cavell case was the reason that von Sauberzweig was supplanted.\nPage: Edith Cavell. Sentence: Edith Louisa Cavell ( ; 4 December 1865 – 12 October 1915) was a British nurse.\nPage: Edith Cavell. Sentence: She was accused of treason, found guilty by a court-martial and sentenced to death.\nPage: Edith Cavell. Sentence: Despite international pressure for mercy, she was shot by a German firing squad.",
