        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "25bbaeda-3061-552c-9d57-3422f0c69b89",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Traugott von Sauberzweig, Edith Cavell\n- Roles: Prussian Generalleutnant, Military Governor of Brussels, British nurse\n- Places: Kassel, Brussels\n- Events: World War I, Edith Cavell's execution, court-martial\n\nFacts:\n- Traugott Martin von Sauberzweig was born on October 28, 1863, and he died on April 14, 1920, in Kassel.\n- Edith Louisa Cavell was born on December 4, 1865, and she was a British nurse.\n- During World War I, Traugott von Sauberzweig was a Prussian Generalleutnant who served on both the Eastern Front and the Western Front in the German Army.\n- In 1915, Traugott von Sauberzweig was the Military Governor of Brussels when Edith Cavell was executed.\n- Edith Cavell was accused of treason, found guilty by a court-martial, and sentenced to death.\n- Despite international pressure for mercy, Edith Cavell was shot by a German firing squad.\n- The Edith Cavell case caused Traugott von Sauberzweig to be supplanted.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "b5503b37-6321-5f8c-8563-5380b8e83942",
        "text": "Page: Traugott von Sauberzweig. Sentence: Traugott Martin von Sauberzweig (October 28, 1863 to April 14, 1920 in Kassel) was a Prussian \"Generalleutnant\" (Lieutenant General) who served on both the Eastern and Western Front in the German Army during World War I.\nPage: Traugott von Sauberzweig. Sentence: In 1915 he had been Military Governor of Brussels in the days of Edith Cavell's execution, and in connection with this tragedy his name was prominently mentioned.\nPage: Traugott von Sauberzweig. Sentence: The Cavell case was the reason that von Sauberzweig was supplanted.\nPage: Edith Cavell. Sentence: Edith Louisa Cavell ( ; 4 December 1865 – 12 October 1915) was a British nurse.\nPage: Edith Cavell. Sentence: She was accused of treason, found guilty by a court-martial and sentenced to death.\nPage: Edith Cavell. Sentence: Despite international pressure for mercy, she was shot by a German firing squad.",
